  "title": "Visual imagery EEG dataset from Gao et al 2026",
  "description": "This dataset contains 32-channel EEG recorded from 22 healthy participants performing visual imagery of ten cued items: animals (dog, bird, fish), geometric figures (pentagram, square, circle), and objects (scissor, watch, cup, chair). Each participant completed up to two sessions of three runs, giving 16,800 trials in total. It is intended for developing visual imagery-based brain-computer interfaces and is distributed in BIDS format with HED event annotations.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 1000 Hz with a Neuracle NeuSenW32 system using 32 Ag/AgCl electrodes placed according to the standard 10-05 montage, with CPz as reference and AFz as ground. Participants imagined image-cued stimuli in 4 s trials across 2 sessions of 3 runs each. Benchmarking used EEGNet and CSP+KNN classifiers with 5-30 Hz bandpass filtering.",
